{title: 215 - The King Shall Come}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #215 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: Ab}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 215}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Cm]The [Fm]King [Cm/G]shall [Ab]come when [Gdim]morning [Eb]dawns
[Cm]And [Fm]light [Gdim]triumphant [Bbm]breaks,
[Ab]When beauty [Cm]gilds [Bbm]the [Ab]eastern [Eb]hills
[Cm]And [Fm]life [Gdim]to [Fm]joy awakes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Cm]Not [Fm]as [Cm/G]of [Ab]old a [Gdim]little [Eb]child,
[Cm]To [Fm]bear [Gdim]and [Ab]fight [Bbm]and [Cm]die,
[Ab]But crowned with [Cm]glory [Ab]like [Eb]the sun
[Cm]That [Fm]lights [Gdim]the [Fm]morning [Gdim]sky.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Cm]O, [Fm]brighter [Ab]than the [Gdim]rising [Eb]morn
[Cm]When [Fm]Christ, [Gdim]victorious, [Cm]rose
[Ab]And left the [Cm]lonesome [Gdim]place [Eb]of death,
[Cm]Despite [Gdim]the [Fm]rage of [Gdim]foes.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[Cm]O, [Fm]brighter [Ab]than that [Gdim]glorious [Eb]morn
[Cm]Shall [Fm]dawn [Gdim]upon [Bbm]our [Cm]race
[Ab]The day when [Cm]Christ in [Ab]splendor [Eb]comes,
[Cm]And [Fm]we [Gdim]shall [Fm]see His [Gdim]face.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 5}
[Cm]The [Fm]King [Cm/G]shall [Ab]come when [Gdim]morning [Eb]dawns
[Cm]And [Fm]light [Gdim]and [Ab]beauty [Cm]brings.
[Ab]Hail, Christ the [Cm]Lord! [Bbm]Your [Ab]people [Eb]pray:
[Cm]Come [Fm]quickly, King of [Gdim]kings.
{end_of_verse}
